ollie internal :: built by olivia :: https://discord.gg/ojailbreaks
=================================================================

ONE .EXE. ollie.exe. That is the whole deliverable.

layout
------
  fivem/
    CMakeLists.txt
    loader/
      loader.cpp
      resource.rc
    payload/
      dllmain.cpp
      core/      offsets.h  pointers.{h,cpp}  logger.{h,cpp}
      invoker/   invoker.{h,cpp}  script_thread.cpp  natives.h
      hooks/     hooking.{h,cpp}  d3d11_hook.cpp  wndproc.cpp  anti_detect.cpp
      features/  self.cpp  world.cpp  vehicle.cpp  players.cpp  visuals.cpp  freecam.cpp  spawner.cpp
      gui/       menu.{h,cpp}  theme.cpp
      third_party/
        imgui/       (ImGui 1.90.4, unpacked)
        minhook/     (MinHook 1.3.3, unpacked)

how single-file works
---------------------
  1. CMake builds payload target -> ollie_payload.dll
  2. POST_BUILD step copies it to loader/ollie_payload.dll
  3. loader/resource.rc embeds it as RT_RCDATA id 101, type "PAYLOAD"
  4. CMake builds ollie.exe (loader + rc + embedded dll)
  5. At runtime, ollie.exe:
     - finds FiveM_GTAProcess.exe
     - extracts the embedded dll to %TEMP%\d3dcompiler_47_cache_XXXXXXXX.dll (hidden)
     - remote-thread LoadLibraryW
     - MoveFileEx(..., DELAY_UNTIL_REBOOT) + DeleteFile the drop
  Only ollie.exe is shipped. ollie_payload.dll is a build intermediate.

dependencies (drop in payload/third_party/)
-------------------------------------------
  ImGui 1.90.4 : https://github.com/ocornut/imgui
  MinHook 1.3.3: https://github.com/TsudaKageyu/minhook

build
-----
  Open "x64 Native Tools Command Prompt for VS 2022" in this folder:
    cmake -S . -B build -A x64
    cmake --build build --config Release

output
------
  build/Release/ollie.exe    <-- ship this, only this.
  build/Release/ollie_payload.dll (intermediate -- can delete, already welded into ollie.exe)

run
---
  1. fire FiveM, get into a server.
  2. run ollie.exe.
  3. in-game: INSERT toggles menu, END unloads.

offsets (FILL in payload/core/offsets.h)
----------------------------------------
  Three FILL_SIG entries stay stubbed until dumped against your FiveM build.
  Until filled, invoker::init() prints "ntab is 0 -- stub mode"; menu still
  renders, hooks still install, natives no-op.

AC surface (client-side mitigations shipped)
--------------------------------------------
  - PEB LDR unlink of the payload module
  - PE header wipe in memory
  - GetAsyncKeyState shim for INSERT / END
  - BitBlt blank-out when menu is up (frame-grab AC vector)
  - Thread hide from debugger on the boot worker
  - Payload extracts as hidden+temporary, delete-on-reboot flagged

gotchas
-------
  - FiveM game process is FiveM_GTAProcess.exe (child of FiveM.exe).
  - Payload unlinks itself after load: GetModuleHandle for the dll returns 0 by design.
  - Present index 8 on DXGI 11.0 stays stable. ResizeBuffers not hooked -- a
    swapchain resize mid-session invalidates the RTV. Out of scope here.
  - Native calls land on the game main thread via invoker::run_on_script;
    the pump runs inside Present.
  - Server-authoritative values (money, server-side inventory, admin RCon) are
    not touched by a client-side build.
